{"BenchmarksToRun":{"binary-v0_0":{"GameName":"Binary","GameDescription":"The binary problem is from the PCGRL framework where the goal is to generate a 2D maze of empty and solid tile where it is fully connected and have a long path in it that is more than the a specific distance. The default value is equal to the width \u002B height of the map.","LevelName":"binary-v0","LevelDescription":"","Tiles":"\r\nTile Character|Tile Name|Tile Description|Minimum Number Of Tile|Maximum Number Of Tiles\r\n---|---|---|---|---\r\n0|Wall|Solid impassable wall for the maze||\r\n1|Floor|Walkable floor for the maze||\r\n","Width":"14","Height":"14","GameType":"TopDown","GameGenre":"Maze","DifficultyLevel":"Easy","HazardLevel":"None","CustomConstraints":"The maze **must** have a minimum path length of 28 steps\nThe map **must** be creative and entertaining \nYou have to use the complete level dimensions to create several areas combinig open with tight areas without violating the path length","TemplateFilePath":"PromptV1.hbs"},"binary-v0_1":{"GameName":"Binary","GameDescription":"The binary problem is from the PCGRL framework where the goal is to generate a 2D maze of empty and solid tile where it is fully connected and have a long path in it that is more than the a specific distance. The default value is equal to the width \u002B height of the map.","LevelName":"binary-v0","LevelDescription":"","Tiles":"\r\nTile Character|Tile Name|Tile Description|Minimum Number Of Tile|Maximum Number Of Tiles\r\n---|---|---|---|---\r\n0|Wall|Solid impassable wall for the maze||\r\n1|Floor|Walkable floor for the maze||\r\n","Width":"14","Height":"14","GameType":"TopDown","GameGenre":"Maze","DifficultyLevel":"Easy","HazardLevel":"None","CustomConstraints":"The maze **must** have a minimum path length of 28 steps\nThe map **must** be creative and entertaining \nYou have to use the complete level dimensions to create several areas combinig open with tight areas without violating the path length","Temp