","GameType":"TopDown","GameGenre":"Maze","DifficultyLevel":"Easy","HazardLevel":"None","CustomConstraints":"The maze **must** have a minimum path length of 42 steps \nThe map **must** be creative and entertaining \nYou have to use the complete level dimensions to create several areas combining open with tight areas without violating the path length","TemplateFilePath":"PromptV1.hbs"},"ddave-v0_0":{"GameName":"Dangerous Dave","GameDescription":"This is a small discrete version of the DOS game Dangerous Dave similar to the one implemented in the PCGRL Framework. Dangerous dave is a small platformer where you need to get a key avoid spikes and collect diamonds and get to exit.","LevelName":"ddave-v0","LevelDescription":"","Tiles":"\r\nTile Character|Tile Name|Tile Description|Minimum Number Of Tile|Maximum Number Of Tiles\r\n---|---|---|---|---\r\n0|Wall|Solid impassable wall||\r\n1|Floor|Walkable floor||\r\n2|Player|The player\u0027s starting position|1|1\r\n3|Exit|The player\u0027s exit for this particular level. This is the goal of the level|1|1\r\n4|Diamond||7|\r\n5|Key|Mandatory prerequisite to be able to unlock the door|1|1\r\n6|Spikes|||22\r\n","Width":"11","Height":"7","GameType":"Platformer","GameGenre":"Puzzle","DifficultyLevel":"Easy","HazardLevel":"Low","CustomConstraints":"The player and exit **must** be above a solid tile.\n\nThe player\u0027s starting position **must** be between: \n - 0 and 11 in X \n- 5 and 7 in Y \nAdditionally, the map exit position **must** be between \n- 0 and 11 in X \n- 0 and 3 in Y.\nThe map **must** also contain a minimum of 2 jumps. \n\n Finally, the map **must** contain between 0 and 7 diamonds distributed across the map.\n\nThe diamonds **must** be reachable.","TemplateFilePath":"PromptV1.hbs"},"ddave-v0_1":{"GameName":"Dangerous Dave","GameDescription":"This is a small discrete version of the DOS game Dangerous Dave similar to the one implemented in the PCGRL Framework. Dangerous dave is a small platformer where you need t